// Test simfile with hand-worked segments, jacks and streams, for calibrating ddr-trainer's
// chart analyzer (src/chart_analyzer.rs), whose tests check the values below. Generated by
// test_resources/make_test_simfiles.py, so edit that instead of this.
//
// One BPM (120, so quarter notes are 0.5 s apart, 8ths 0.25 s and 16ths 0.125 s), no stops.
//
// Patterns are only looked for inside a segment: a run of notes with no gap longer than
// 0.25 s between two of them, since a longer break gives the player time to reset their feet.
// 8th notes here are exactly 0.25 s apart, so they stay in one segment, while a dotted 8th
// (0.375 s) or longer gap starts a new one.
//   - a jack is a note that steps on an arrow the note right before it in the same segment
//     also stepped on (hold heads count). So a run of 4 notes on one arrow is 3 jacks, a jump
//     on the same two arrows as the jump before it is 1, and repeats across a break aren't
//     jacks
//   - jacks per second is jack speed, not density: for each jack, how many jacks there are
//     from it up to (but not including) 1 s later, within its segment. The statistics are the
//     mean, median and max of those counts, or 0 with no jacks
//   - a stream is a segment of at least 8 notes, and its length is how many notes it has
//
//   chart      segments (notes in each)  jacks  jacks/s: mean     median  max
//   Beginner   none                          0           0          0       0
//   Easy       5 9 2                         8           19/8       2       5
//   Medium     7 8 19 1                      0           0          0       0
//   Hard       20                           10           34/10      3       7
//   Challenge  1 1 1 1 16 6 1                4           5/4        1       2
//
//   chart      streams  length: mean  median  max
//   Beginner   0        0             0       0
//   Easy       1        9             9       9
//   Medium     2        13.5          13.5    19
//   Hard       1        20            20      20
//   Challenge  1        16            16      16
//
// Each chart's jacks, by time in seconds, with how many jacks the second from each holds
// (| starts a new segment):
//   Easy       at 0.25 0.75 | 2.125 2.25 2.5 2.625 2.75 | 3.25,  holding 2 1 | 5 4 3 2 1 | 1
//   Hard       at 0.125 0.25 ... 0.875 2.25 2.5 2.75,  holding 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 3 2 1
//   Challenge  at 2.75 4.75 | 6.375 6.625,  holding 1 1 | 2 1
// The windows stop at the end of their segment: in Easy, the jack at 3.25 would otherwise add
// to the windows from 2.5, 2.625 and 2.75.
#TITLE:Pattern Stats;
#ARTIST:ddr-trainer;
#MUSIC:pattern_stats.ogg;
#OFFSET:0.000000;
#BPMS:0.000=120.000;
#STOPS:;

